{
  "_comment": [
    "A login prompt on the system console.",
    "",
    "Named for the pairing rather than the program: login is not inherently a",
    "console service, it is a terminal logon originator that this seed happens",
    "to point at /dev/console. A second prompt on /dev/tty1 would be another",
    "seed with another TTYPath and another service name -- which is the whole",
    "reason TTYPath carries a path rather than a boolean.",
    "",
    "TTYPath does two things. It attaches the terminal to stdin/stdout/stderr,",
    "and it makes peinit put the service in its own session owning that",
    "terminal as its controlling tty (setsid + TIOCSCTTY, before exec). The",
    "second is what login actually needs: without a controlling terminal there",
    "is no job control, and a logon shell without job control is broken in ways",
    "that only show up later. login also attempts this itself and tolerates",
    "EPERM precisely because peinit is expected to have done it first.",
    "",
    "Requires lpsd, not authd. authd being up means a prompt can be COLLECTED;",
    "lpsd being up means it can be ANSWERED. Ordering on the authority alone",
    "opens a window where the prompt appears and every attempt fails with",
    "AuthorityUnavailable. lpsd requires authd, so this orders after both.",
    "",
    "Triggers on boot:settled, not boot. peinit writes its progress to",
    "/dev/console and login writes its prompt to the same device, so a prompt",
    "started mid-boot gets written over: login emits 'Username: ' with no",
    "newline and blocks, peinit appends a service line, and the result is",
    "unreadable until the user presses Enter and login redraws. boot:settled",
    "waits for the boot set to stop moving -- or five seconds, whichever comes",
    "first, so a hung service costs a delay rather than the prompt.",
    "",
    "It is a trigger and not a Requires edge because it is a scheduling",
    "preference, not a dependency: login does not need a quiet boot to work, it",
    "just looks broken without one. What it genuinely needs is lpsd, which is",
    "what Requires says below.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Alive (1): login never sends READY=1, so Notify would hold",
    "the boot until the start timeout expired and then fail a service that is",
    "sitting at a working prompt.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is Always (2): logging out, or a failed attempt that exits,",
    "must yield a fresh prompt rather than a dead console. OnFailure would not",
    "respawn on a clean exit, which is the ordinary way a session ends.",
    "",
    "ErrorControl stays Normal (0), unlike authd and lpsd. Those two are",
    "Critical because a system that cannot authenticate has not booted; this is",
    "one prompt on one terminal, and a machine that comes up with a broken",
    "console but a working authority is still reachable and still worth",
    "booting.",
    "",
    "TERM=vt220 rather than linux: a console that is a serial line is the",
    "common case for this image (console=ttyS0). An image whose console is a",
    "real VT wants its own seed, or an EnvVars override.",
    "",
    "Attaching a terminal suppresses output capture -- the pipes eventd would",
    "read are closed -- so nothing this service prints reaches the logs. That is",
    "correct for an interactive prompt and worth knowing when debugging one.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the login package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an image",
    "names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\login-console",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath",     "type": "sz",    "data": "/bin/login" },
        { "name": "TTYPath",       "type": "sz",    "data": "/dev/console" },
        { "name": "Triggers",      "type": "multi", "data": ["boot:settled"] },
        { "name": "Requires",      "type": "multi", "data": ["lpsd"] },
        { "name": "Identity",      "type": "sz",    "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness",     "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 2 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl",  "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "Environment",   "type": "multi", "data": ["TERM=vt220"] },
        { "name": "DisplayName",   "type": "sz",    "data": "Console login" },
        { "name": "Description",   "type": "sz",    "data": "Terminal logon prompt on the system console" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
